    art: 
    arrival: 'Captain Morrow: Captain Elias Morrow, of the Lark.

      A room with
      water, if you please. And no attics. Too far from the sea.'
    story:
    - 'Captain Morrow[sad]: Every night I watch the lake. The Lark should have been
      home by now.'
    - 'Captain Morrow: There''s a lantern on the far shore some nights. Could be
      her. Could be anyone.'
    - 'Captain Morrow: I found my logbook in the lake-view room. The last page...
      I never read it.'
    - 'Captain Morrow[happy]: "All hands safe ashore." They made it. They made it
      home.

      I think I can stop waiting now.'
    checkout: 'Captain Morrow[happy]: Take my compass, keeper. It always points to
      what''s hidden.'
    keepsake: Brass Compass
